{
  "title": "structural_tag tool-name guard does not bind the second tool call in \
a response",
  "description": "`magebench.pilot.tool_name_guard` builds a \
`structured_outputs.structural_tag` that permits exactly the tool names a seat was \
offered, so an invented function name cannot be emitted. Measured on vLLM 0.27.1 \
(`--tool-call-parser qwen3_coder --enable-auto-tool-choice`), the tag IS enforced — \
but only on the first tool call of a response.\n\
\n\
HOW IT WAS MEASURED (job 7866, three arms, N=8 each, one 4B checkpoint):\n\
  * unguarded                       0/8 invented a name (clean baseline)\n\
  * guarded with the REAL tool names 8/8 ordinary tool calls (the healthy state — a \
server that mangled every tag would fail here)\n\
  * guarded to a tag permitting ONLY `zzz_enforcement_probe`, a name in no toolset \
and no prompt: 3/8 emitted it, 5/8 returned no tool call at all\n\
\n\
The forced name is unforgeable — it exists only inside the tag — so its appearance \
proves the serving engine applies the tag.\n\
\n\
THE DEFECT. In all 3 draws where the forced name appeared, a SECOND parsed tool \
call carried `get_action_choices`, which that tag does not permit:\n\
\n\
    tool_calls: [ zzz_enforcement_probe  args={} ,\n\
                  get_action_choices     args={\"choice\": \"choice\"} ]\n\
    content:    \"...Let me call get_action_choices to see what actions I can take.\"\n\
\n\
The model intended `get_action_choices`; the grammar overrode the first slot and the \
second came through unaltered. A name the guard forbade reached the parsed output.\n\
\n\
NOT DETERMINED: whether the second trigger occurrence is unconstrained, or the \
parser is more lenient than the grammar and split one malformed emission into two. \
Deciding needs the raw pre-parse string, which the chat-completions endpoint does \
not expose — `message.content` holds only prose once the parser has consumed the \
tool-call text. That is why this is filed rather than fixed.\n\
\n\
WHY IT MATTERS AND FOR WHOM. On the 35B teacher this is small: 4.7% of responses in \
job 7860 carry two tool calls ({0:34, 1:1209, 2:62}), every observed second name is \
one of the six real tools, and at the 35B's measured invention rate of 3.77e-5 per \
call those 207 second slots expect 0.008 inventions — so zero there is no evidence \
either way, not reassurance. On the 4B students it is the blocker: hallucinated tool \
names are their characteristic fatal failure (7 of 8 policy deaths in job 4452), so \
'the guard binds EVERY tool call in a response' is a precondition for any 4B run \
under the guard.\n\
\n\
SUGGESTED ACCEPTANCE TEST for a fix, which the current guard would fail: repeat the \
fake-name arm and require the forced name in EVERY slot of a multi-call response, or \
require the response to carry exactly one tool call. `pipelines/eval/prove_guard_\
enforced.py` in the mtg repo is the harness.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
